OneiOS 5001: build the AIR frontend of Jesvi-iOS (its tools/mesa/air-frontend.patch) as part of Mesa.

src/compiler/air is userland/metal-amd/air of OneiOS, copied there by
userland/metal-amd/air/build.sh: the frontend that reads Apple's shader bitcode (AIR) and makes NIR.
This patch is only the meson line that reaches it; a tree without the directory builds as before
(Jesvi's patch had no guard: its build scripts always copied the directory first).

diff --git a/src/compiler/meson.build b/src/compiler/meson.build
index 68f0832..6500233 100644
--- a/src/compiler/meson.build
+++ b/src/compiler/meson.build
@@ -65,6 +65,12 @@ subdir('nir')
 
 subdir('spirv')
 
+# OneiOS (userland/metal-amd/air): the AIR frontend of Jesvi-iOS, copied here by
+# userland/metal-amd/air/build.sh. A tree without it builds as before.
+if fs.is_dir('air')
+  subdir('air')
+endif
+
 if with_clc
   subdir('clc')
 endif
